@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2105 = private unnamed_addr constant [19 x i8] c"binary-op-exception", align 1
@anon.0de5ee8f4a9046f07397637c35d34c13.2106 = private unnamed_addr constant [557 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `except` clauses that attempt to catch multiple\0Aexceptions with a binary operation (`and` or `or`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA binary operation will not catch multiple exceptions. Instead, the binary\0Aoperation will be evaluated first, and the result of _that_ operation will\0Abe caught (for an `or` operation, this is typically the first exception in\0Athe list). This is almost never the desired behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    pass\0Aexcept A or B:\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    pass\0Aexcept (A, B):\0A    pass\0A```\0A", align 1
